each whose body copies a field of the element, in the forward direction,
where the element has another field: the copy is the whole target element, so
nothing can move or drop the other field, and the forward lens must account
for it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...close({id!: string, is_enabled!: bool})]
})
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...string]
})

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
	}
}

BackwardLens: {
	v1_0: _
	v0_0: {
		u: _each(v1_0.u, {id: _item, is_enabled: true})
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0347]: 0.0 declares u[].is_enabled, and the _each copying _item.id maps nothing else of the element
 --> 1.0.thema:8:20
  |
8 |         u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
  |                          ^^^^^
  |
  = note: an _each whose body is a copy has nowhere to move or drop the rest of the element, and the forward lens must account for every field the source declares
